<title>UK: Eurostar operator appoints new chief executive.</title>
<headline>Eurostar operator appoints new chief executive.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-09-06</dateline>
<text>
<p>London &amp; Continental Railways, the consortium awarded the contract to operate the Eurostar high- speed passenger train service through the Channel Tunnel, said on Friday it was appointing Adam Mills chief executive.</p>
<p>Mills, 53, was the deputy chief executive of National Express Group Plc and had been seconded from the UK coach and airport facilities company since June.</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44 171 542 4017</p>
